One way is to keep your character's level as low as possible (i.e.,
somewhere at Exp:14 or slightly above, but not much more). Archons don't
appear unless you reach a certain level (IIRC Exp:30 but I may be
wrong).

The way I play, I usually shun wraith corpses and save !oGL's for
ascension run purposes, and get my HP boost using other methods (such as
alchemy). But this requires careful planning, since you'll have less
skill slots to spend so you can't afford to make a mistake earlier in
the game.

As for conducts... I've only tried a few, and I think the easiest is
probably no PM/polypiling. Genocideless also isn't too bad if you're
properly prepared to deal with L's and (M)MF's. If you have Magicbane +
MR, L's are merely annoying rather than deadly. Wishless is also
manageable if you know how to make the best of the equipment you find
(altho I b0rked my last potentially wishless ascension by a stupid
mistake at the Castle, and then by not being prepared properly for Plane
of Air---had to burn a good number of wishes).  I've been trying
weaponless / pacifist, but couldn't get past the initial game.
Vegetarian / vegan is hard in the initial game (unless you're a
tourist), and makes it hard to get resistances. I haven't figured out
how to work with illiterate / atheist / foodless.


